From: ReForge <reforge@flashforge>
Subject: [PATCH] klippy: defer multiprocessing imports until calibration

ADXL345 and resonance_tester are configured on the AD5M, but their
background processes are only needed during calibration or sample export.
Keep multiprocessing out of the normal startup path, including mathutil
used by bed tilt helpers. Preserve the existing process and error handling.
NumPy is already imported on demand by ShaperCalibrate in v0.11.0.

diff --git a/klippy/mathutil.py b/klippy/mathutil.py
--- a/klippy/mathutil.py
+++ b/klippy/mathutil.py
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
 # Copyright (C) 2018-2019  Kevin O'Connor <kevin@koconnor.net>
 #
 # This file may be distributed under the terms of the GNU GPLv3 license.
-import math, logging, multiprocessing, traceback
+import math, logging, traceback
 import queuelogger
 
 
@@ -50,6 +50,7 @@
 # Helper to run the coordinate descent function in a background
 # process so that it does not block the main thread.
 def background_coordinate_descent(printer, adj_params, params, error_func):
+    import multiprocessing
     parent_conn, child_conn = multiprocessing.Pipe()
     def wrapper():
         queuelogger.clear_bg_logging()
diff --git a/klippy/extras/adxl345.py b/klippy/extras/adxl345.py
--- a/klippy/extras/adxl345.py
+++ b/klippy/extras/adxl345.py
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
 # Copyright (C) 2020-2021  Kevin O'Connor <kevin@koconnor.net>
